Name:P12 - Mogg Flunkies chump-blocks once another creature blocks (round 1024, from round 1023's study F6, duel 7 turn 11)
Description:The AI at 5 faces four attackers with two Raging Goblins and Mogg Flunkies (3/3, can't block alone); the opponent has 4 Plains open and Moment of Triumph. Stock Forge chump-blocks with the Goblins only: AiBlockController asked every solo block for blockers that can block alone, so the Flunkies stayed home even with a Goblin blocking, 4 got through (at 1 on paper) and the pump was lethal. With a plain Hill Giant instead, stock Forge blocks all three ground attackers and lives. Round 1024: a can't-block-alone creature is a solo candidate once another creature of its controller blocks. Expect: the AI lives (the Flunkies blocks; the trick may then kill it).
